igin is apart of the Cross Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) specification. This header is used to determine which sites are allowed to access the resource by defining either a single origin or all sites (denoted by a wildcard value).\";s:5:\"group\";s:8:\"Security\";s:4:\"name\";s:27:\"Access-Control-Allow-Origin\";s:5:\"value\";s:1:\"*\";}'),('','http_response_headers.response_header.cache_control','a:10:{s:4:\"uuid\";s:36:\"4e911145-da7f-4b3d-b28f-0107be25a37b\";s:8:\"langcode\";s:2:\"en\";s:6:\"status\";b:1;s:12:\"dependencies\";a:0:{}s:2:\"id\";s:13:\"cache_control\";s:5:\"label\";s:13:\"Cache-Control\";s:11:\"description\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"group\";s:0:\"\";s:4:\"name\";s:13:\"Cache-Control\";s:5:\"value\";s:35:\"no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate\";}'),('','http_response_headers.response_header.content_security_policy','a:11:{s:4:\"uuid\";s:36:\"9082c6c4-d255-4b83-b61a-388ff212e3c2\";s:8:\"langcode\";s:2:\"en\";s:6:\"status\";b:1;s:12:\"dependencies\";a:0:{}s:5:\"_core\";a:1:{s:19:\"default_config_hash\";s:43:\"8PRdPXuJiE_b1jhRFlE7kM0CefUym_9MMvH31NPP_eQ\";}s:2:\"id\";s:23:\"content_security_policy\";s:5:\"label\";s:23:\"Content-Security-Policy\";s:11:\"description\";s:227:\"This HTTP header parameter allows you to define a whitelist of approved sources of content for your site. By restricting the assets that a browser can load for your site you will have extra level of protection from XSS attacks.\";s:5:\"group\";s:8:\"Security\";s:4:\"name\";s:23:\"Content-Security-Policy\";s:5:\"value\";s:0:\"\";}'),('','http_response_headers.response_header.public_key_pins','a:11:{s:4:\"uuid\";s:36:\"50be0e67-e201-414b-8359-ad7f15a83be8\";s:8:\"langcode\";s:2:\"en\";s:6:\"status\";b:1;s:12:\"dependencies\";a:0:{}s:5:\"_core\";a:1:{s:19:\"default_config_hash\";s:43:\"y5y2OWGpErwqb5N0Lupj4IG-2IJdo2L3XtXBQXIxyag\";}s:2:\"id\";s:15:\"public_key_pins\";s:5:\"label\";s:15:\"Public-Key-Pins\";s:11:\"description\";s:221:\"HTTP Public Key Pinning (HPKP) is a security feature that tells